   "date": "2018-03-14T02:38:06Z",
   "subject": "Error in CODEX2 (negative widths are not allowed)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Hi YuChao,</div><div><br></div><div>I am using CODEX2 to detect CNV for my WES data without normal controls.  </div><div><br></div><div>I wrote a loop to call CNV for chromosomes, one by one successively (1...22,X,Y).  <b>The program worked with chr1 and chr2, but something weird just happened when run getcoverage() for chr3</b>.  The detailed information is as below.</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">&gt;   coverageObj &lt;- getcoverage(bambedObj, mapqthres = 20)  </span></div></div><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">Error in .Call2(&quot;solve_user_SEW0&quot;, start, end, width, PACKAGE = &quot;IRanges&quot;) : </span></div></div><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">  solving row 1: negative widths are not allowed</span></div></div><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">Calls: getcoverage ... RangesList -&gt; IRanges -&gt; solveUserSEW0 -&gt; .Call2 -&gt; .Call</span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>I tried to output the <b>bambedObj$ref </b>to check the width, and found <b>all values of width are &gt;=2</b>.  File<b> chr3_ref</b> was attached. </div><div><br></div><div>For now, I have no idea about how to fix it.  The <b>Rscript CODEX2.R</b> was also attached for your convenience. </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot for your time. Have a good day.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Sincerely,</div><div><br></div><div>Caiyun</div><div><br></div><div> </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M9ATT4DSAgAJ",
   "from": "Caiyun Zhu",
   "author": "02e54964b579b6bf",
   "date": "2018-03-14T10:31:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: Error in CODEX2 (negative widths are not allowed)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Sorry for inconvience, I find the mistake after ...nearl 6 hours.  The bedFile.bed should be sorted by start and end positions, take care of the info author mentioned!</div><div><br></div><div>1. Seeking the source code of getcoverage.R (<a href=\"https://rdrr.io/bioc/CODEX/src/R/getcoverage.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/bioc/CODEX/src/R/getcoverage.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243851505000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0EUNWS69iDMJjJe0GO4iui\">https://rdrr.io/bioc/CODEX/src/R/getcoverage.R</a>).</div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">    st <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">&lt;-</span> <a href=\"https://rdrr.io/r/stats/start.html\" style=\"box-sizing:inherit;background:0px 0px;color:rgb(65,131,196)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/r/stats/start.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243851505000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1XgXmHVQXuk8MO_7J73LQD\">start</a><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">(</span>ref<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">)[</span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">]  #the first start pos of $ref</span>\r\n    ed <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">&lt;-</span> <a href=\"https://rdrr.io/r/stats/start.html\" style=\"box-sizing:inherit;background:0px 0px;color:rgb(65,131,196)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/r/stats/start.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243851505000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1XgXmHVQXuk8MO_7J73LQD\">end</a><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">(</span>ref<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">)[</span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(0,128,0)\"><a href=\"https://rdrr.io/r/base/length.html\" style=\"box-sizing:inherit;background:0px 0px;color:rgb(65,131,196)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/r/base/length.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243851505000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ez-rbAtzq6Kv3DldUWZ3b\">length</a></span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">(</span>ref<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">)]  #the last end pos of $ref</span>\r\n     .......    </pre><pre style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">    IRanges<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">(</span>st <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">10000</span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">,</span> ed <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">+</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">10000</span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">))  #if the st-10000 &lt; ed + 10000, the error will occur.</span></pre><pre style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\"><br></span></pre><pre style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">2. Sort the bedFile.bed and run all chromosomes again.</span></pre><pre style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;padd